// World milli-unit coordinate -> grid cell (the inverse of worldmap.id's
// world_x_of_cell/world_z_of_cell). world_x_of_cell(gx) centers cell gx at
// gx*S - (W*S)/2 + S/2, so the boundary between cell gx-1 and cell gx sits
// at gx*S - (W*S)/2; shifting wx by +(W*S)/2 before the integer divide by S
// lands any point in [that boundary, next boundary) on cell gx (truncating
// division rounds toward zero, which is floor for these always-nonnegative
// shifted values, since 0 <= gx < W).

cell_x(int wx) {
} return int (wx + (grid_w() * spacing()) / 2) / spacing();

cell_z(int wz) {
} return int (wz + (grid_h() * spacing()) / 2) / spacing();
